From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aquarat <3090997+aquarat@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:29:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 30/34] pmdomain: apple: pmp-report: Use a 64-bit shift for the
 entry bit

The PS-REQ/PS-ACK words are 64 bits wide, but the entry's bit was made
with "1 << ent->id", an int shift. That is undefined for ids of 31 and
above, which t6002 uses for its second die's display entries (0x33,
0x34). Use BIT_ULL().

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: aquarat <3090997+aquarat@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
index 39a10a0b6..2d60a4a48 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
@@ -119,7 +119,7 @@ static int apple_pmp_report_set_state(struct generic_pm_domain *genpd, bool enab
 {
 	struct apple_pmp_report_entry *ent = genpd_to_apple_pmp_report_entry(genpd);
 	struct apple_pmp_report *rep = dev_get_drvdata(ent->dev->parent);
-	u64 bit_val = 1 << ent->id;
+	u64 bit_val = BIT_ULL(ent->id);
 	u64 val;
 	unsigned long flags;
 
-- 
